    "executive_summary": "A total of 595 disaster incidents were reported across multiple jurisdictions, aggregated from USGS (261) and NOAA (334) data sources. The events span a diverse range of categories, prominently featuring seismic activity with numerous earthquake recordings, alongside widespread meteorological advisories, warnings, and watches such as small craft advisories, gale warnings, and extreme heat warnings. Urgency levels are predominantly classified as Low (238) and Minor (230), with 79 moderate, 41 severe, and 4 high-urgency incidents. Representative high-severity incidents include several moderate-magnitude earthquakes internationally, notably in Vanuatu, Argentina, and the Philippines. Given the distribution and variety of the active alerts, continued monitoring of seismic developments and localized weather hazards is recommended to ensure public safety.",
    "recommendations": [
        "Continue real-time monitoring of seismic activity across international and domestic reporting zones.",
        "Maintain active watches on marine and coastal areas affected by small craft advisories and gale warnings.",
        "Disseminate heat and severe weather advisories to populations in high-risk regional zones."
    ]
